  "notes": "The dialogue that opens the Preface, sung by priest and people. Its own document because it is a fixed exchange the reader looks up by name, and because everything after it changes with the day. CORDA at w008 is accusative with no verb expressed: the missal's Sursum corda is an elliptical command, and the response supplies the verb (habémus). SURSUM at w007 is the adverb, not a preposition — it governs nothing. DÓMINO DEO NOSTRO at w016-w016 is a dative and its apposition, tagged as such; witness do prints a comma between them, adjudicated in the apparatus with the corpus rulings on appositions.",
